---
import { siteConfig } from "../config";
---

--

<header
  id="header"
  class="fixed top-0 left-0 right-0 z-50 hidden md:block transition-all duration-300"
>
  <nav class="max-w-7xl mx-auto px-8 py-4">
    <ul class="flex items-center gap-8 justify-center">
      <li>
        <a
          href="/"
          class="text-gray-700 hover:text-[var(--brand-green)] transition-colors font-medium"
        >
          Home
        </a>
      </li>
      
    </ul>
  </nav>
</header>

<script>
  window.addEventListener("scroll", () => {
    const header = document.getElementById("header");
    if (window.scrollY > 100) {
      header?.classList.add("bg-white/80", "backdrop-blur-sm");
    } else {
      header?.classList.remove("bg-white/80", "backdrop-blur-sm");
    }
  });
</script>

<style>
  html {
    scroll-behavior: smooth;
  }
</style>



<section id="about" class="p-8 sm:p-12 md:p-16 lg:p-24">
  <div>
    <div class="grid grid-cols-1 lg:grid-cols-12 gap-8 lg:gap-16 items-start">
      <div class="lg:col-span-4">
        <h2
          class="text-3xl sm:text-4xl md:text-5xl xl:text-7xl font-bold text-gray-900"
        >
          Patterns
        </h2>
        <div
          class="w-[75px] h-[5px] mt-2 rounded-full"
          style={`background-color: ${siteConfig.accentColor}`}
        >
        </div>
      </div>

      <div class="lg:col-span-8 space-y-8">
        <section class="space-y-5" aria-labelledby="pattern-examples-title">
          <div>
            <h3 id="pattern-examples-title" class="text-2xl sm:text-3xl font-bold text-gray-900">
              Six patterns at a glance
            </h3>
            <p class="mt-2 text-base sm:text-lg leading-relaxed text-gray-600">
              The candle bodies show open-to-close movement; the thin lines show each period’s high and low. These simplified drawings illustrate the shapes, not a trading recommendation.
            </p>
          </div>

          <div class="grid grid-cols-1 sm:grid-cols-2 gap-5">
            <article class="rounded-2xl border border-slate-200 bg-white p-5 shadow-sm">
              <h4 class="text-xl font-bold text-gray-900">Doji · indecision</h4>
              <svg class="mt-3 w-full h-auto" viewBox="0 0 320 180" role="img" aria-labelledby="doji-title doji-desc">
                <title id="doji-title">Doji candlestick illustration</title>
                <desc id="doji-desc">One candle with a very small body between longer upper and lower wicks, showing that open and close are nearly equal.</desc>
                <line x1="160" y1="24" x2="160" y2="146" stroke="#587086" stroke-width="4" stroke-linecap="round" />
                <rect x="143" y="78" width="34" height="7" rx="2" fill="#8b6f47" />
                <line x1="78" y1="82" x2="130" y2="82" stroke="#b8c5d1" stroke-width="1.5" stroke-dasharray="5 5" />
                <line x1="190" y1="82" x2="242" y2="82" stroke="#b8c5d1" stroke-width="1.5" stroke-dasharray="5 5" />
                <text x="160" y="169" text-anchor="middle" fill="#526174" font-size="14" font-family="system-ui, sans-serif">Open ≈ close</text>
              </svg>
              <p class="mt-2 text-sm leading-relaxed text-gray-600">
                The opening and closing prices are nearly the same, leaving a tiny body. A doji can signal a pause or uncertainty; by itself, it does not confirm a reversal.
              </p>
            </article>

            <article class="rounded-2xl border border-slate-200 bg-white p-5 shadow-sm">
              <h4 class="text-xl font-bold text-gray-900">Bullish engulfing · possible reversal</h4>
              <svg class="mt-3 w-full h-auto" viewBox="0 0 320 180" role="img" aria-labelledby="engulfing-title engulfing-desc">
                <title id="engulfing-title">Bullish engulfing candlestick illustration</title>
                <desc id="engulfing-desc">A smaller red bearish candle is followed by a larger green bullish candle whose body extends beyond the first candle's body.</desc>
                <line x1="105" y1="28" x2="105" y2="132" stroke="#587086" stroke-width="4" stroke-linecap="round" />
                <rect x="88" y="51" width="34" height="38" rx="2" fill="#df6b6b" />
                <line x1="213" y1="38" x2="213" y2="146" stroke="#587086" stroke-width="4" stroke-linecap="round" />
                <rect x="196" y="42" width="34" height="66" rx="2" fill="#4d9b73" />
                <line x1="79" y1="51" x2="241" y2="51" stroke="#b8c5d1" stroke-width="1.5" stroke-dasharray="5 5" />
                <line x1="79" y1="89" x2="241" y2="89" stroke="#b8c5d1" stroke-width="1.5" stroke-dasharray="5 5" />
                <text x="105" y="169" text-anchor="middle" fill="#526174" font-size="14" font-family="system-ui, sans-serif">Earlier</text>
                <text x="213" y="169" text-anchor="middle" fill="#526174" font-size="14" font-family="system-ui, sans-serif">Next</text>
              </svg>
              <p class="mt-2 text-sm leading-relaxed text-gray-600">
                A bullish candle’s body fully covers the previous bearish body. Traders often study it after a decline as a possible shift in momentum; context and follow-through matter.
              </p>
            </article>

            <article class="rounded-2xl border border-slate-200 bg-white p-5 shadow-sm">
              <h4 class="text-xl font-bold text-gray-900">Hammer · possible bullish reversal</h4>
              <svg class="mt-3 w-full h-auto" viewBox="0 0 320 180" role="img" aria-labelledby="hammer-title hammer-desc">
                <title id="hammer-title">Hammer candlestick illustration</title>
                <desc id="hammer-desc">A small green body near the top of the candle with a long lower wick and a short upper wick.</desc>
                <line x1="160" y1="35" x2="160" y2="146" stroke="#587086" stroke-width="4" stroke-linecap="round" />
                <rect x="143" y="49" width="34" height="22" rx="2" fill="#4d9b73" />
                <text x="160" y="169" text-anchor="middle" fill="#526174" font-size="14" font-family="system-ui, sans-serif">Long lower wick</text>
              </svg>
              <p class="mt-2 text-sm leading-relaxed text-gray-600">
                A small body sits near the high, with a much longer lower wick. After a decline it may suggest buyers pushed prices back up; confirmation is important.
              </p>
            </article>

            <article class="rounded-2xl border border-slate-200 bg-white p-5 shadow-sm">
              <h4 class="text-xl font-bold text-gray-900">Bearish engulfing · possible reversal</h4>
              <svg class="mt-3 w-full h-auto" viewBox="0 0 320 180" role="img" aria-labelledby="bear-engulf-title bear-engulf-desc">
                <title id="bear-engulf-title">Bearish engulfing candlestick illustration</title>
                <desc id="bear-engulf-desc">A smaller green bullish candle is followed by a larger red bearish candle whose body extends beyond the first candle's body.</desc>
                <line x1="105" y1="39" x2="105" y2="143" stroke="#587086" stroke-width="4" stroke-linecap="round" />
                <rect x="88" y="71" width="34" height="38" rx="2" fill="#4d9b73" />
                <line x1="213" y1="32" x2="213" y2="140" stroke="#587086" stroke-width="4" stroke-linecap="round" />
                <rect x="196" y="53" width="34" height="66" rx="2" fill="#df6b6b" />
                <line x1="79" y1="71" x2="241" y2="71" stroke="#b8c5d1" stroke-width="1.5" stroke-dasharray="5 5" />
                <line x1="79" y1="109" x2="241" y2="109" stroke="#b8c5d1" stroke-width="1.5" stroke-dasharray="5 5" />
                <text x="105" y="169" text-anchor="middle" fill="#526174" font-size="14" font-family="system-ui, sans-serif">Earlier</text>
                <text x="213" y="169" text-anchor="middle" fill="#526174" font-size="14" font-family="system-ui, sans-serif">Next</text>
              </svg>
              <p class="mt-2 text-sm leading-relaxed text-gray-600">
                A bearish candle’s body fully covers the previous bullish body. After an advance it may suggest momentum is changing, but the pattern alone cannot predict what follows.
              </p>
            </article>

            <article class="rounded-2xl border border-slate-200 bg-white p-5 shadow-sm">
              <h4 class="text-xl font-bold text-gray-900">Morning star · three-candle turn</h4>
              <svg class="mt-3 w-full h-auto" viewBox="0 0 320 180" role="img" aria-labelledby="morning-star-title morning-star-desc">
                <title id="morning-star-title">Morning star candlestick illustration</title>
                <desc id="morning-star-desc">A long red candle, a small-bodied candle lower in the range, and a green candle recovering into the first candle's body.</desc>
                <line x1="72" y1="28" x2="72" y2="119" stroke="#587086" stroke-width="4" stroke-linecap="round" />
                <rect x="56" y="40" width="32" height="57" rx="2" fill="#df6b6b" />
                <line x1="160" y1="103" x2="160" y2="143" stroke="#587086" stroke-width="4" stroke-linecap="round" />
                <rect x="144" y="112" width="32" height="13" rx="2" fill="#8b6f47" />
                <line x1="248" y1="47" x2="248" y2="132" stroke="#587086" stroke-width="4" stroke-linecap="round" />
                <rect x="232" y="62" width="32" height="55" rx="2" fill="#4d9b73" />
                <text x="72" y="169" text-anchor="middle" fill="#526174" font-size="13" font-family="system-ui, sans-serif">Decline</text>
                <text x="160" y="169" text-anchor="middle" fill="#526174" font-size="13" font-family="system-ui, sans-serif">Pause</text>
                <text x="248" y="169" text-anchor="middle" fill="#526174" font-size="13" font-family="system-ui, sans-serif">Recovery</text>
              </svg>
              <p class="mt-2 text-sm leading-relaxed text-gray-600">
                A long bearish candle is followed by a small-bodied pause and then a strong bullish candle. It is studied as a possible shift after a decline, not a guarantee.
              </p>
            </article>

            <article class="rounded-2xl border border-slate-200 bg-white p-5 shadow-sm">
              <h4 class="text-xl font-bold text-gray-900">Evening star · three-candle turn</h4>
              <svg class="mt-3 w-full h-auto" viewBox="0 0 320 180" role="img" aria-labelledby="evening-star-title evening-star-desc">
                <title id="evening-star-title">Evening star candlestick illustration</title>
                <desc id="evening-star-desc">A long green candle, a small-bodied candle higher in the range, and a red candle falling into the first candle's body.</desc>
                <line x1="72" y1="61" x2="72" y2="146" stroke="#587086" stroke-width="4" stroke-linecap="round" />
                <rect x="56" y="75" width="32" height="55" rx="2" fill="#4d9b73" />
                <line x1="160" y1="31" x2="160" y2="71" stroke="#587086" stroke-width="4" stroke-linecap="round" />
                <rect x="144" y="45" width="32" height="13" rx="2" fill="#8b6f47" />
                <line x1="248" y1="48" x2="248" y2="136" stroke="#587086" stroke-width="4" stroke-linecap="round" />
                <rect x="232" y="58" width="32" height="55" rx="2" fill="#df6b6b" />
                <text x="72" y="169" text-anchor="middle" fill="#526174" font-size="13" font-family="system-ui, sans-serif">Advance</text>
                <text x="160" y="169" text-anchor="middle" fill="#526174" font-size="13" font-family="system-ui, sans-serif">Pause</text>
                <text x="248" y="169" text-anchor="middle" fill="#526174" font-size="13" font-family="system-ui, sans-serif">Pullback</text>
              </svg>
              <p class="mt-2 text-sm leading-relaxed text-gray-600">
                The opposite sequence—a long bullish candle, small pause, and strong bearish candle—is studied as a possible shift after an advance. Context and confirmation matter.
              </p>
            </article>
          </div>
        </section>


        <div class="space-y-5 text-lg sm:text-xl leading-relaxed text-gray-600">
          <p>
            A candlestick summarizes price movement over a set period. Its body shows the opening and closing prices, while its wicks mark the high and low. Candlestick patterns are recognizable arrangements of one or more candles—such as a doji, engulfing pattern, or morning star—that traders study for clues about momentum, indecision, or a possible reversal. They are signals to investigate, not guarantees of what the market will do next.
          </p>
          <p>
            This project turns those chart-reading rules into a repeatable research workflow. It scans historical stock prices for configurable patterns across symbols, compares what happened over the following 1–12 trading sessions, and presents date-, symbol-, and industry-filtered reports with charts. The goal is to explore and compare how patterns behaved across historical data at scale, rather than manually inspect charts one by one; past results do not predict future returns.
          </p>
        </div>


